Suggested qualification after full-checkout application:
  git apply --check scripts/patches/gh518-ordinary-retry-recovery.patch
  cargo test --locked --lib search::query::retry_budget::tests
  cargo test --locked --test logging search_logs_backend_selection
  cargo fmt --check

Scope: only a larger optional fetch after a nonempty filtered native page can
recover. An initial failure, an empty post-filter page, cancellation, corruption,
or another non-fuel error still propagates. First-required-query archive fallback
and a shared whole-request fuel allowance are outside this candidate.

The fragmented regression uses a normal reader for the valid page and a separate
one-unit reader for a genuine typed retry refusal. It does not establish natural
count/retry-only exhaustion under one common budget or reproduce reporter latency.

